WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:10.720
In 1965, researchers cut the forest on one small watershed at Hubbard Brook, New

2
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:14.440
Hampshire. They used herbicide so nothing grew back.

3
00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:20.560
Soon its stream carried far more nitrate than the stream of an uncut watershed

4
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:24.240
nearby. The nitrogen had been there all along.

5
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.040
Cutting the trees changed where it went.

6
00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:29.320
How would you know where it goes?

7
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:34.640
Keep accounts for nitrogen, the way a bank keeps accounts for money.

8
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:40.440
A pool is the amount held in one place at one time, like a balance.

9
00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:45.080
A flux is a transfer, like a deposit or a withdrawal.

10
00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:49.500
Draw a boundary, and choose an interval, such as a year.

11
00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:51.800
Then one rule holds.

12
00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.040
Change in stock equals inputs minus outputs.

13
00:00:56.933 --> 00:00:58.933
Take an invented forest.

14
00:00:59.733 --> 00:01:04.693
These numbers are illustrative, in kilograms of nitrogen per hectare per year.

15
00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:08.233
Deposition from the air brings in 8.

16
00:01:09.153 --> 00:01:10.593
Fixation brings in 6.

17
00:01:11.353 --> 00:01:13.113
The stream carries out 3.

18
00:01:14.473 --> 00:01:17.593
Denitrification returns 2 to the air as gas.

19
00:01:18.693 --> 00:01:21.573
Inputs are 14. Outputs are 5.

20
00:01:22.313 --> 00:01:25.533
The forest gains 9, stored in wood and soil.

21
00:01:26.417 --> 00:01:33.657
Inside the boundary, the soil organic nitrogen pool holds 4,500 kilograms per hectare.

22
00:01:34.597 --> 00:01:37.857
Decomposers release 90 of it each year as ammonium.

23
00:01:38.637 --> 00:01:39.637
Plants take it up.

24
00:01:40.197 --> 00:01:42.957
That flux is about six times the inputs.

25
00:01:43.477 --> 00:01:45.317
Yet it never appeared in the sum.

26
00:01:46.277 --> 00:01:49.897
An output of one pool is an input of another, so they cancel.

27
00:01:51.097 --> 00:01:53.337
Cancelling does not mean turnover is small.

28
00:01:53.337 --> 00:01:55.477
Here it is the largest flux.

29
00:01:56.417 --> 00:01:59.817
Now cut the forest and suppress regrowth.

30
00:02:00.657 --> 00:02:01.877
Plant uptake stops.

31
00:02:02.857 --> 00:02:07.637
Decomposers keep releasing ammonium, and nitrifiers turn it into nitrate.

32
00:02:08.717 --> 00:02:11.557
Soil holds nitrate weakly, so it washes out.

33
00:02:12.757 --> 00:02:17.457
Suppose stream export rises to 40, and the other terms stay fixed.

34
00:02:18.397 --> 00:02:19.857
Outputs are now 42.

35
00:02:20.837 --> 00:02:25.297
The change is 14 minus 42, a loss of 28.

36
00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:28.150
That size is invented.

37
00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:34.610
At Hubbard Brook, stream losses of nitrate and of cations such as calcium rose well

38
00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:36.410
above those of the uncut reference.

39
00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.110
The real result shows the direction.

40
00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:41.490
The nitrogen was always there.

41
00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:43.850
What changed was where it went.

42
00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:51.030
Keep the rule. Change in stock equals inputs minus outputs, for a stated boundary and interval.
